413	150,1420,775,1952 - 620,1420,780,1670	413. Half of a Cranberry-blossom, magnified.	A Cranberry blossom cut in half and magnified: four narrow petals turned sharply back, the long stamens and single style standing up from the dotted ovary with its cells below.
414	390,760,1168,1660 - 390,1420,615,1660 - 855,1405,1020,1582	414. A Checkerberry plant, or Aromatic Wintergreen.	A Checkerberry plant: a short upright stem from a creeping rootstock, with a few oval leaves and small white urn-shaped flowers nodding beneath them.
415	855,1405,1020,1582	415. Slice across the "berry," and the pod inside.	The Checkerberry fruit sliced across: a thick fleshy ring around the five-celled pod, with small seeds in each cell.
